WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.280
There are many different misconceptions in
life.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.280
Many.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.440
And one of the things misconceptions tend
to do is they tend to prevent people from

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.960
doing things that could benefit them.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.880
They say things like, "Oh my God, I don't
know if I want to do this" because in their

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.120
mind, this is what they believe, so they don't
do it.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:21.360
So the definition of a misconception, the
meaning of misconception is a thought or an

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:27.000
opinion that is incorrect because it is based
on faulty thinking or understanding.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.820
So today, I want to clarify some of the misconceptions
of entrepreneurship.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.050
I'm right now at College Station, Texas, which
is the home of the Aggies, Texas A&amp;M University.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.129
These guys invited me to come and speak to
their next class of entrepreneurs.

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:41.219
They have a program here called Entrepreneurship
Society.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:45.589
And last time when I was talking to these
young, aspiring entrepreneurs, they had so

00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:46.670
many different misconceptions.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.870
I have nine of them I want to share with you.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:49.870
So the first one is this.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.360
Here's one of the biggest misconceptions that
I keep hearing about.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.629
Entrepreneurs are born.

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:55.629
Constantly.

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:56.629
Entrepreneurs are born.

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:00.949
You are born an entrepreneur, which is an
absolute lie, if there ever was one.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:05.150
Yes, it's like saying one is born with a forty
inch vertical leap.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.490
Yes, you're right.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:10.510
Larry Bird did not have a 40-inch vertical
leap, so he cannot dunk like LeBron James.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:11.510
Yes.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.710
But that doesn't mean you are born to be a
basketball player, and Larry Bird is not.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.240
That has no meaning.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.680
Michael Jordan was born to be a basketball
player.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.340
But Steph Curry was not, because he's 6'1"
170 pounds.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.530
You can't say that because he's a tiny guy.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.100
Muggys Bogues was a 5' 3" basketball player.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.730
5' 3" and he played the NBA, nearly ten something
years, and he was pretty good at it.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.610
So the same goes to saying this person is
not meant to be an entrepreneur because he's

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.610
too shy.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.659
This person's not meant to be an entrepreneur
because he had a 1.8 GPA in high school.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:45.450
This person's not meant to be an entrepreneur
because he's a certain nationality or color

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.450
of skin.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.450
No.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.450
Don't buy it.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.450
It's misconceptions.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.799
Someone's trying to persuade you, that you
can't become an entrepreneur and it's not

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:52.799
the truth.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:54.649
It's faulty thinking, and you need to question
it.

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:58.740
You don't need to just say, "Oh, this guy
on YouTube said that entrepreneurs are born."

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.740
BS.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.740
Don't buy it.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.740
It's a misconception.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.840
#2: The second thing is something I struggled
with is, you have to cheat or steal, to win

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.840
as an entrepreneur.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.840
You do not.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.390
You do not have to cheat or steal as an entrepreneur.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.650
I've watched this for many, many years with
my business.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.680
I had to compete and some people did it the
right way, some people did it the wrong way.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.620
Some people had shortcuts and every single
time there's a shortcut, we're tempted.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.620
Everybody's tempted.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:24.620
I was tempted.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.800
Every time, I'm sitting here competing against
a guy that's making 400 grand a month, and

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.390
I'm only making 30 grand a month, and I'm
25 years old, whatever it is, 26 years old.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:36.040
And he's doing certain things that I don't
want to do.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.190
But if I have to compete with him, I have
to do that to compete with him.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.260
I didn't do it, he kept doing it.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.720
He lost his licenses.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.720
We kept going.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.410
Now if I would have done it, I would have
also lost my license.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.550
You do not have to cheat or steal to win in
business.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.550
You don't.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.540
You do not have to cheat or steal to win in
business.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.631
People say that, because it is a way out for
them to say, I chose not to be an entrepreneur

00:02:57.631 --> 00:02:59.730
because I am a noble human being.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:03.970
And because I'm a noble human being, I refuse
to cheat, because it's against my character.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:04.970
That is not true.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.710
You don't have to cheat or steal to become
an entrepreneur.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.390
There are laws, you break them, you're going
straight to prison.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.070
#3: They got lucky.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.070
This whole lucky thing.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.110
And by the way, I talk about lucky quite a
lot.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.210
On one end, luck doesn't happen accidentally.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:26.700
For example, nobody is going to go on a date
with a beautiful girl by not talking to her.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.840
You have to take action.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.730
There's got to be a conversation.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.560
No one closes a big sale, without knowing
anything about their products, because the

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.450
bigger the sale it is, the more educated the
customer is.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.170
You can't just go to a customer and ask for
a $200,000 check and they're going to say

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:42.410
yes and you know nothing about your product.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.260
It's not going to happen.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.760
You have to work your butt off to become an
expert.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.070
You have to immerse yourself on it.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:52.111
You're going to go through certain breaking
points that you don't feel like doing anything,

00:03:52.111 --> 00:03:53.760
and you want to throw in the towel.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.690
Those moments are things that people don't
see.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.540
Nobody sees I'm in Hilton right now.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.580
And I remember one time we were on the tour
last year when we were doing the entrepreneurship

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:01.580
tour.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:08.680
We stopped by Conrad Hilton where he accidentally
bought this building, it was a hospital?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.680
It was something.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.700
It wasn't a hotel, right?

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.030
He bought this thing, he turned it into a
hotel.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.600
Next thing you know, it started growing.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.650
There's Hiltons in Iran.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.109
And I'm in Iran, I've gone to a Hilton when
I was a kid growing up, Hilton was like insane.

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:22.500
We don't know the stories of when Hilton almost
went out of business.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.820
We don't know the stories of his arguments
with his wife.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.990
We don't know the times where he's at a hotel
room by himself away from a kid's birthday

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.650
because he has to be at a business meeting,
and he's absolutely feeling crap about the

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.740
fact that he missed an event for his kid or
. . you don't know those moments.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.190
So you can't say they got lucky.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.490
There is luck involved in business.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.340
I'm not telling you there isn't.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.870
Nothing wrong with getting lucky.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.650
But there's got to be a lot of hard work before
you get lucky.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.840
#4: Selfish.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.639
Entrepreneurs are selfish.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:49.639
Entrepreneurs are selfish.

00:04:49.639 --> 00:04:52.870
You'll hear the word selfish, greedy, and
all they care about is money, quite regularly.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.009
They're selfish.

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:55.009
They're very selfish.

00:04:55.009 --> 00:04:56.009
They're all selfish.

00:04:56.009 --> 00:04:57.009
All they care about is themselves.

00:04:57.009 --> 00:04:58.009
Listen.

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:01.930
You can't build a billion dollar company - when
you build a billion dollar company, the guy

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:05.599
that built a billion dollar company, he doesn't
keep the billion dollars.

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:10.390
The billion dollar company, he probably keeps
a fifty million dollar salary per year, let's

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.770
just say if you build a billion dollar company.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.909
Now if you own a big part of it, sure.

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:15.599
The value of the company is yours.

00:05:15.599 --> 00:05:20.219
But if your company grows to a billion dollars
per year, he takes $50 million a year income.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.550
Even people say that's greedy.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.509
Let's say he takes a $50 million a year income,
because I'm picking a the greediest CEO you

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:25.550
can think about.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.289
He's taking a $50 million a year income, he
built a billion dollar company, okay?

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:30.879
Where does that $950 million go to?

00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:31.879
You tell me.

00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:33.270
Does that go in his pocket?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.270
No.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.270
It goes to what?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.270
It goes to employees, it goes to healthcare.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.270
It goes to building.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.270
It goes to a lease.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.270
It goes to construction.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.479
It goes to long communication, Internet, servers.

00:05:41.479 --> 00:05:44.069
These are all jobs being created.

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:51.110
A billion dollar empire is creating $950 million
dollars of revenue to other people that lead

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.379
to taxes.

00:05:52.379 --> 00:05:56.659
You can't be selfish and build a big company.

00:05:56.659 --> 00:05:57.659
You just cannot.

00:05:57.659 --> 00:06:01.550
You can be selfish and be a salesperson, because
all you're doing is selling and it's all you,

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.539
one person show, one-man show, because it's
all about you.

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:04.539
Yes, you can be selfish.

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:05.810
I agree with you.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:08.319
It's impossible for you to build an empire
being selfish.

00:06:08.319 --> 00:06:11.979
It's mathematically impossible for you to
build a big empire being selfish.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:14.330
The math doesn't make sense.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.380
You can't win an NBA championship without
having assist.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.400
You can't.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.520
It's never happened, and it's never going
to happen.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:25.789
You can't win a baseball game without having
somebody that's double playing the team, catches

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:26.789
the ball.

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:27.789
You can't have it.

00:06:27.789 --> 00:06:28.789
You can't have a no hit.

00:06:28.789 --> 00:06:30.129
I can go on with any different sport.

00:06:30.129 --> 00:06:33.009
You cannot do it without having a team that's
selfish.

00:06:33.009 --> 00:06:34.340
It just does not work.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.840
It is not going to work that way.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.279
Not in the world of business.

00:06:37.279 --> 00:06:39.080
#5: All you need is a great idea and product.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.409
A lot of people message me and say, "Pat,
guess what, man."

00:06:41.409 --> 00:06:42.409
What's that?

00:06:42.409 --> 00:06:43.990
"Man, I've got this product, you and I need
to team up.

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:44.990
It's a billion dollar idea.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.189
I promise you, bro.

00:06:46.189 --> 00:06:47.189
You're going to be a billionaire.

00:06:47.189 --> 00:06:48.189
You can do this."

00:06:48.189 --> 00:06:52.059
I'm like, you really think ideas are what
makes a billion dollar.

00:06:52.059 --> 00:06:55.229
. you think the idea is what makes it a billion
dollars?

00:06:55.229 --> 00:06:56.229
Really?

00:06:56.229 --> 00:06:57.319
You think an idea is?

00:06:57.319 --> 00:06:59.270
An idea means nothing.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.389
Nothing.

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:01.630
You know why?

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.800
Because very few execute.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:04.900
Very few execute.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.909
And here's another thing about ideas.

00:07:06.909 --> 00:07:11.169
There are many crappy products in the world
that are sold on the shelves of Wal-Mart.

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:12.479
Many.

00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:16.300
There are many crappy products in the world
that are sold at Macy's and people buy.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.020
And their products suck.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:24.039
There are many shirts that you go buy, where
the strings are out with the shirt.

00:07:24.039 --> 00:07:25.039
It's just terrible.

00:07:25.039 --> 00:07:26.039
People buy them.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:27.039
Why do they buy?

00:07:27.039 --> 00:07:30.639
So your idea that you have, means nothing
if there's no execution.

00:07:30.639 --> 00:07:31.810
An idea's just an idea.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.669
There are many great ideas out there.

00:07:33.669 --> 00:07:35.300
Execution is the issue.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.840
#6: All you need is to raise capital.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.870
People say, Pat, if I raise money, man - like
last time one kid was asking me, "I'm telling

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.770
you, if I had a million dollars right now,
I'd do this."

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.639
If I heard, every single time somebody told
me "if I had a million dollar investment,"

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:47.889
I'd be a billionaire today.

00:07:47.889 --> 00:07:50.439
Everybody wants to talk about if they had
money and raised capital.

00:07:50.439 --> 00:07:51.949
It means nothing.

00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:53.159
It means nothing.

00:07:53.159 --> 00:07:54.190
It does mean a little bit.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.190
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:55.190 --> 00:08:00.039
But you're not going to get a - I get messages,
"Pat, can you do a video on how to raise capital?"

00:08:00.039 --> 00:08:01.331
I'll do a video on how to raise capital.

00:08:01.331 --> 00:08:03.199
Can you do a video on how to raise capital?

00:08:03.199 --> 00:08:04.570
Can you do a video on how to raise capital?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:05.570
I will.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.570
I'll definitely do that.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.360
"Because if I have the capital, I'll do this,
this, this with my business."

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.360
And I'll tell them.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.629
I'll say, have you ever wanted a pass before?

00:08:12.629 --> 00:08:13.629
Who are you?

00:08:13.629 --> 00:08:14.629
How hard do you work?

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:15.779
What's your track record?

00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:16.840
What relationships do you have?

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.259
What associations do you have?

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:19.259
Who needs to bet on you?

00:08:19.259 --> 00:08:20.259
Would you bet on you?

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:21.300
Why should someone bet on you?

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.740
If you can answer those questions, you'll
eventually raise capital.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.970
If you don't have that, you ain't getting
capital.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.169
It's that simple.

00:08:28.169 --> 00:08:32.940
Your reputation and track record and the relationships
and the associations who validate you, will

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.460
attract the capital.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.250
If you don't have this, there is no capital.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.250
It's simple.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.479
You have to have a lot of this on the front
end, to get the money.

00:08:40.479 --> 00:08:46.870
#7: They all had great initial connections,
because it's all about the contacts and connections.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:50.720
My connections were guys who went to the nightclub
on a weekly basis.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.940
My connections were guys who were chasing
skirts.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:57.830
My connections were my boys and we'd sit down
and talk sports all day long and you know,

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:03.950
play spades or play whatever cards, play all
these other games.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:04.950
That's my connections.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:05.950
So who are my connections?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.810
I didn't go to university to be part of an
alumni.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.070
What are my connections?

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:12.410
My connections from the military never ever
introduced me to anybody in business.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.620
These are my connections from military.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.700
They don't have a business background.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.760
Who are my connections?

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:20.010
Connections are a by-product of a lot of work,
of people seeing you saying, "This guy's legit.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.040
He's working hard.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.610
Let's connect him to this person."

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.750
It's not, Hey, this person had a father who's
related to Vanderbilt and.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:27.750
. . no.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.870
It does not work that way.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.060
If you have that, it's an edge.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.060
I had zero.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.690
My parents have never been entrepreneurs.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.100
I don't come from a business background.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:37.170
My dad stopped going to school after 8th grade
to help support his family.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.140
I'm not the smart kid on campus.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.140
Nothing.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.140
None of that stuff.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.750
I had to work my tail off to get my connections.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.970
If you're looking for shortcuts, misconception.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.950
#8: It's a massive risk.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.640
I've got to take such a massive risk.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:53.250
This is why I don't want to become an entrepreneur.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.170
I've seen so many people lose everything and
all this other stuff.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:57.170
Yes.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:58.170
There are a lot of people that lose everything.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.170
You're right.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:00.790
There are a lot of people that go all in.

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:04.730
And we always want to watch on YouTube guys
who go all in, who what?

